          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वाहक — vāhak — \"a bus conductor\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वाहकाने माझं तिकीट तपासलं. vāhakāne mājhaṁ tikīṭ tapāslaṁ. The conductor checked my ticket."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "On a bus the चालक (cālak) drives and the वाहक (vāhak) sells and checks tickets."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वाहक (vāhak) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit vāhaka, \"one who carries, a carrier\" (Monier-Williams); on a bus it names the conductor."
            }
          ]
        },
