        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: चालवणे",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चालवणे — cālavṇe — \"to drive; to run\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "माझे काका बस चालवतात. mājhe kākā bas cālavtāt. My uncle drives a bus."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with -ने (he …): त्याने चालवलं, tyāne cālavlaṁ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Not the same as चालणे, to walk: चालवणे (cālavṇe) is to make something go, so गाडी चालवणे (cālavṇe) is to drive and दुकान चालवणे (cālavṇe) is to run a shop."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चालवणे (cālavṇe) is built on चालणे, \"to walk, to go\", which CDIAL lists as Marathi ċālṇẽ under calyati, \"goes\" (CDIAL 4721), as its causative: to make a vehicle or a business go."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
